	cserver :
			= static void add_res(struct result_buffer *resbf, char *rrn, ShortInt ret, char *scroll_no = NULL)
				- it is used to add result into result buffer
				- RRN, return code and scroll no are added into result buffer

			= void init_dispDtl(struct Dispute_Detail *dispDtl)
				- sets balnk values to all fields in Dispute_Detail object

			= ShortInt validate_atmDispute(struct request_buffer *reqbf, struct result_buffer *resbf,
					vector <struct Dispute_Detail> *v)
				- it reads one shortInt named rowcount which indicates total no. of records sent from client side
				- it sends error in following cases :
					- if request is not from head office branch then it returns with error ONLY_HEAD_BR
					- if user has no permission to PASS record, if not then returns with error ERR_USR_NPERMIT
					- if record contains RRN then
						- search related record in ATMLOG with the help of tsetl_dt, rrn, tr_amt_
							if exact record not found then generate error
						- if record found but account no. is not valid then generate error
						- if (atoi(alog.ret_batch) > 0) means dispute is already given then generate error
					- if record not found in ATMLOG
					- if any record does not contain RRN and account no. is valid
				- if flag = true means, record is valid then it get stored into vector
				- finally after parsing every record if flag is false and vector contains any record
					 then clear the vector and return error otherwise if flag is true then return with OK

			= void update_atmLog(struct trnf_scr trscr, vector < struct Dispute_Detail > v)
				- for every scroll in TRNF_SCR if tran_amt_dc == 'C', then find respective record in ATMLOG
				- RRN is fetched from tran_part and transactino date from Dispute_Detail
				- only successful transaction with msg_type = "0200" are considered for updation
				- when a particular record from ATMLOG with above condition found, then modify following fields
					memtozstr(trs.tran_amt, alog.rdue_amt, ellen [TRAN_AMT]);
					- transaction date(dispute date) is copied into ret_date
					- dispute report date is copied into rptdate
					- dispute settlement date is copied into settle_dt
					- dispute due date is copied into due_date
					- transaction batch no. (Dispute batch no.) is copied into ret_batch
					- lien_type indicates whether dispute is F/P (i.e Full / Partial)
					- aquirer institution code is copied into sifsc code
					- destination institution code is copied into difsc code
					

			= ShortInt add_atmDispute(struct request_buffer *reqbf, struct result_buffer *resbf)
				- check whether buffer is valid or not using validate_atmDispute() function
				- if valid then do following procedure else return with error
				- if result buffer is not NULL then set OK(0) to indicate result is OK,
					set error pointer which is initially 0 and increament size of result
				- then record added into transfer scroll (TRNF_SCR)
				- every record from vector added into scroll
				- if amount is to be credited then
					- narration will be "ECOR RRN DD/MM/YYYY"
					- settle_date is copied into tdt
				- if amount is to be debited then narration will be "RUPAY DISPUTE DD/MM/YYYY-cycle_no"
				- add tranasfer scroll using add_trscroll() function
				- batch no of first record is copied into batchno
				- batch is passed using pass_batch_trasfer
				- then atmlog is updated for every RRN using update_atmLog()

			= ShortInt del_atmDispute(struct request_buffer *reqbf, struct result_buffer *resbf)
				- it reads branch code, transaction date and batch no. from request buffer
				- if result buffer is not NULL then set OK(0) to indicate result is OK,
					set error pointer which is initially 0 and increament size of result
				- check whether user has deletion permission, if not then returns with error ERR_USR_NPERMIT
				- finds transfer scroll with first key
				- if scroll is already deleted then return with error ALRDY_DEL
				- else if transaction amount dc flag is 'C' then,
					- read  rrn from tran_part of transaction ( trs.tran_part+5)
					- with the help of cheque date and rrn find respective record from ATMLOG 
					- if record with same date and rrn found, and message type is 0200 and response code is 00
						then set following fields to blank.
						RET_DATE,  RPTDATE, SETTLE_DT, DUE_DATE, RET_BATCH, LIEN_TYPE, SIFSCCODE, DIFSCCODE

				- after modifying ATMLOG, again find transfer scroll and respective TRAN and
					call del_trnf() function to delete transaction

			= void atmDispute_handler(struct request_buffer *reqbf)
				- depend on operation code it invokes either add_atmDispute or del_atmDispute
					which in turn process request and send result.